      "hints": [
        "Combine over common denominator $\\sin^2\\theta - \\cos^2\\theta$.",
        "Simplify numerator to $\\sin^2\\theta + \\cos^2\\theta$.",
        "Divide numerator and denominator by $\\cos^2\\theta$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Combine the fractions on the left-hand side over the common denominator $(\\sin\\theta + \\cos\\theta)(\\sin\\theta - \\cos\\theta)$:\n$$\\frac{\\sin\\theta(\\sin\\theta - \\cos\\theta) + \\cos\\theta(\\sin\\theta + \\cos\\theta)}{(\\sin\\theta + \\cos\\theta)(\\sin\\theta - \\cos\\theta)}$$",
        "Expand the numerator and denominator:\n$$= \\frac{\\sin^2\\theta - \\sin\\theta\\cos\\theta + \\sin\\theta\\cos\\theta + \\cos^2\\theta}{\\sin^2\\theta - \\cos^2\\theta} = \\frac{\\sin^2\\theta + \\cos^2\\theta}{\\sin^2\\theta - \\cos^2\\theta}$$",
        "Divide every term in the numerator and denominator by $\\cos^2\\theta$:\n$$= \\frac{\\frac{\\sin^2\\theta}{\\cos^2\\theta} + \\frac{\\cos^2\\theta}{\\cos^2\\theta}}{\\frac{\\sin^2\\theta}{\\cos^2\\theta} - \\frac{\\cos^2\\theta}{\\cos^2\\theta}}$$",
        "Apply the identity $\\tan\\theta = \\frac{\\sin\\theta}{\\cos\\theta}$ to conclude:\n$$= \\frac{\\tan^2\\theta + 1}{\\tan^2\\theta - 1}$$"
      ],
      "checking": {
        "mode": "ai",
        "ai_rubric": {
          "Trigonometric Identities": "Combines over common denominator (M1). Obtains $\\frac{\\sin^2\\theta+\\cos^2\\theta}{\\sin^2\\theta-\\cos^2\\theta}$ and divides by $\\cos^2\\theta$ (DM1). Obtains $\\frac{\\tan^2\\theta+1}{\\tan^2\\theta-1}$ (A1)."
        },
        "criteria_source": "mark_scheme_structured"
